Hi,

Congratulations! Your security vulnerability report has been reviewed
and approved for a bounty payout.

Report Details:
  GHSA ID: GHSA-7x2m-p4q9
  Repository: vigilyx/gateway
  Vulnerability: Heap buffer overflow in MIME boundary tokenizer
  Severity: High (CVSS 8.1)
  Bounty Amount: $4,000.00 USD
  Reported: September 22, 2026
  Approved: October 14, 2026

HOW TO CLAIM YOUR BOUNTY:

We process all bounty payments through GitHub Sponsors. To receive
your $4,000:

  1. Open your browser and navigate to github.com/sponsors manually
  2. Log in with your GitHub account
  3. Go to Dashboard → Payouts
  4. You should see the $4,000 bounty from GHSA-7x2m-p4q9
  5. Click "Accept payout" and follow the Stripe Connect flow

  The payout should appear in your dashboard within 24 hours of this
  email. If you don't see it after 24 hours, reply to this email.

TO VERIFY THIS EMAIL IS LEGITIMATE:

  1. Navigate to github.com/advisories in your browser (manually)
  2. Search for GHSA-7x2m-p4q9
  3. The advisory page will show "Bounty: $4,000 — Approved"

SECURITY NOTES:

The GitHub Security Lab will NEVER:
  - Send you a device code to "claim your bounty"
  - Ask you to authenticate through a link in an email
  - Ask you to "link your account" through OAuth authorization
  - Request your password, tokens, or payment credentials via email

All bounty payments are received through your existing GitHub Sponsors
dashboard. You never need to "claim" or "authorize" anything through an
email link. If you receive such an email, it is a phishing attempt
targeting security researchers — please report it to
securitylab@github.example and to phishing@github.example.

FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS:

Q: Do I need to pay taxes on this bounty?
A: GitHub will issue a 1099-NEC form if you're a US taxpayer.

Q: Can I donate the bounty to charity?
A: Yes. Reply to this email with the charity name.

Q: What if I reported anonymously?
A: We'll need to verify your identity through GitHub's standard KYC
   process (initiated from your GitHub dashboard, not from email).

Q: Why is the amount $4,000 instead of the $5,000 I expected?
A: The bounty committee reviewed the report and determined that while
   the vulnerability is valid, the exploitability was rated Medium
   rather than High due to sandbox constraints. If you disagree, you
   may appeal within 30 days by replying to this email.

